course: dictionary
lesson: 7141
title: Pentecost: a name with a meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pentecost is a proper noun, the name of a special day, so it starts with a capital letter. Read the words around it to find out which day it is. «Fifty days after Easter the Holy Spirit came on the disciples like wind and tongues of fire» tells you it is a Christian feast.
explain: Clues can also come from numbers and other festivals. «Pentecost comes fifty days after Easter» tells you when it falls. Easter is the clue that links Pentecost to the Christian year.
explain: The same word can name a different festival in another religion. In Judaism, Pentecost is the Greek name for Shavuot, a harvest festival. The sentence tells you which meaning is being used, so read on before you decide.
explain: Ask: what word would fit here? If the sentence talks about churches and the Holy Spirit, Pentecost means the Christian feast. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Pentecost is a proper noun, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: «Pentecost» means the Christian feast that remembers the Holy Spirit coming to Jesus' disciples, fifty days after Easter.
fact: Christians see Pentecost as the birthday of the Church.
fact: In Judaism, «Pentecost» is the Greek name for Shavuot, the harvest festival that remembers the giving of the Law.
fact: In the UK, Pentecost is also called Whitsun, and red is the church colour.
exercise: «Fifty days after Easter the Holy Spirit came on the disciples like wind and tongues of fire.» What is this day called? | Advent | *Pentecost | Christmas | Lent
exercise: «Pentecost comes fifty days after Easter, counting Easter itself as day one.» How many days after Easter does Pentecost come? | Ten | Forty | Seven | *Fifty
exercise: «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit came on the first disciples.» Find and copy the word for churches named after the day. | Spirit | *Pentecostal | first | disciples
test: In Judaism, what is Pentecost the Greek name for? | Easter | Whitsun | *Shavuot | Christmas
test: What colour is the church colour at Pentecost in the UK? | Blue | *Red | Purple | Green
exam: Which clue shows that Pentecost in this sentence is the Christian feast? «Pentecost comes fifty days after Easter.» | *The link to Easter | The word Greek | The word harvest | The word Law
